// jsonNumberCmp compares a JSON number against a decimal literal exactly,
// answering -1, 0 or 1 as the number is less than, equal to or greater than the
// literal.
//
// Exactly is the point: this is what every numeric keyword on an exactly held
// number is enforced through, and a comparison made in float64 would give the
// value and the bound one reading between them wherever they differ past the
// 53rd bit. It is also what makes 1.50 equal to 1.5 and 1e2 equal to 100, which
// a comparison of the literals as text would not.
