// jsonNumberIsMultipleOf reports whether v is an exact multiple of m.
//
// Both are decimals, so the question is whether one integer divides another
// once the two scales are lined up: v is Dv*10^sv and m is Dm*10^sm, and v/m is
// a whole number exactly when Dm divides Dv*10^(sv-sm). The float64 quotient
// this replaces was compared against a tolerance of 1e-9, which called
// 4611686018427387905 a multiple of 4611686018427387904 -- the two share a
// float64 -- and would call any large enough pair of neighbours the same.
//
// Neither power of ten is ever built. A positive difference of scales is folded
// into the divisor by modular exponentiation, and a negative one is decided by
// length first: a divisor with more digits than the dividend divides nothing
// but zero.
