// sides of every comparison come out of the same function: a schema's member
// and an instance are put through identical code, and there is no second
// implementation in the generator for the two to drift apart. A literal that
// somehow cannot be read is kept exactly as the schema wrote it, which can only
// ever match a document that reads back the same way.
